ology  can attend school so if all the kids who  didn't have laptops came in what would  that mean  i might as well just open my doors you  know we've  provided 30 i think so far  to a school of 180 in our mainstream  boat i've got to make this is safe for  the children who come in  and the safe for the teachers as well  another primary school in the gateshead  area kelvin grove sent a notice to  parents  saying classes are oversubscribed and is  exploring criteria for setting  caps on who can come in this pandemic  has served to remind us that schools  aren't just places of education  they offer help with social care  counseling  meals mental health support all things  that many children need  more than ever gateshead mom to lupe  cecile worries about her children's  development  her primary school isn't offering online  learning and what's more a native  nigerian she struggles to teach the  english phonics papers set by the school  and being on a low income heating and  food is another concern they keep  opening the fridge  like mom and we have snacks and we have  snacks  then there was a time i was asking them  do you hit like this in school  with increased demand on the fridge  several families who would normally be  taking their kids to chopwell primary  school  are instead queuing outside the  community center next door  here at the pickle palace you pay what  you can afford for leftovers from the  supermarkets  the working poor isn't it sort of  they're at that sort of level where the  conquest food bank but they still  struggle to sort of  you know fill the cupboards every week  or can i have a  turkey month please other local  charities agree the working poor and  their children  are being hardest hit by school closures  low income families  a lot of them they're in this band where  they miss out  on that support and that help they're  just over the barrier to getting things  like free school meal vouchers  they have to pay the increased demands  on gas and electric  themselves and they're on very very low  wages  this community in gateshead exemplifies  the problems facing the whole country  they're struggling with the lockdown but  they're also fearful  of the virus jason farrell sky news
 

